    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nRenaming a **folder** in the 'mini.files' explorer renames it on disk, but LSP-aware import/reference updates in other files do not happen — imports keep pointing to the old folder path.\nRenaming a single **file** the same way works correctly (imports are updated). Reproduced with ts_ls (typescript-language-server 5.3.0), which does support folder renames.\n\n**Expected behavior**: renaming a folder sends `workspace/willRenameFiles` with the folder's old/new URIs, so returned workspace edits update importers.\n\n**What might be happening.** I have zero knowledge of Neovim internals — this analysis comes from an LLM, so treat it as a hint. \nIt points at `H.lsp_fs_hook()`:\n\n    -- Precompute LSP file type for filters (path can be not yet on disk)\n    file.fs_type = (d.from or d.to):find('/$') ~= nil and 'folder' or 'file'\n\nFor rename/move/delete, `d.from` comes from the path index, which never stores trailing slashes — so every such entry is labeled `'file'`. A renamed folder then fails both of ts_ls's filters (no matching extension for the `file` glob; mislabeled for the `folder` one) and is dropped from `params.files`, so the server receives an empty rename list. Checked with a stub client advertising ts_ls's exact filters: `request_sync` received `params.files = {}` for a folder rename, a populated list for a file rename. If correct, the `willDelete`/`didDelete` hooks are affected the same way.\n\n\n\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory with the standard 'init.lua' from the template, adding:\n\n    ```lua\n    require('mini.files').setup()\n    MiniDeps.add('neovim/nvim-lspconfig')\n    vim.lsp.enable('ts_ls')\n    ```\n\n   (requires `typescript-language-server` in PATH: `npm i -g typescript typescript-language-server`)\n\n2. Create a minimal TS project:\n\n    ```bash\n    mkdir -p /tmp/ts-repro/utils && cd /tmp/ts-repro\n    echo '{}' > package.json\n    echo \"export const x = 1\" > utils/a.ts\n    echo \"import { x } from './utils/a'\" > main.ts\n    ```\n\n3. `cd /tmp/ts-repro && NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim main.ts`, wait for ts_ls to attach (`:checkhealth vim.lsp`).\n\n4. `:lua MiniFiles.open()`, rename `utils` to `helpers` in the explorer buffer, press `=` and confirm.\n\n**Observed**: the folder is renamed on disk, but the import in 'main.ts' still reads `'./utils/a'` (broken). No LSP edit is applied.\n\n**Expected**: import is updated to `'./helpers/a'`.\n\n**Control**: renaming only the *file* `utils/a.ts` → `utils/b.ts` the same way updates 'main.ts' correctly, which confirms LSP file operations are otherwise working.",
